}
``

Wait — but with `.md`-first, would a DIRECTORY named `*.md` be misread? Not a real case here (dirs don't end .md instructions/). And files that are NOT .md (none under instructions/ currently? R1/R2 walk js files too? v1ShimIndex only needs .md shims; non-.md files (e.g. .js) fall to the descent branch — file_exists on a file is truthy → walk(file) → file_list null → entries [] → harmless no-op. Fine — same as the original R13 behavior pre-split presumably. Let me check git history of this function to confirm the ORIGINAL order at 980ac31a9 (the "sensor worked" commit).

